
public class Solution extends GuessGame {
    public int guessNumber(int n) {
        // Initialize search range
        int left = 1;      // smallest possible number
        int right = n;     // largest possible number

        // Binary search loop
        while (left <= right) {

            // Find middle safely (avoids overflow)
            int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;

            // Call the provided API
            int res = guess(mid);

            // If guess is correct
            if (res == 0) {
                return mid;
            }
            // If our guess is higher than the picked number
            else if (res == -1) {
                right = mid - 1;   // search in left half
            }
            // If our guess is lower than the picked number
            else {
                left = mid + 1;    // search in right half
            }
        }

        // This case should never happen if input is valid
        return -1;
    }
}
⏱️ Time Complexity
O(log n)
Each step cuts the search space in half (binary search).
Maximum number of iterations ≈ log₂(n)
🧠 Space Complexity
O(1) (constant space)
No extra data structures are used—just a few variables.
